      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-09T02:39:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well the context is not in this patch. It should be explained. That\u0027s expected regardless, and doubly so because BUG\u003dnone which provides 0 context.\n\nI\u0027m not understanding the issue. \"kernel is sleeping but the system hasn\u0027t entered s0ix\" --  Why not? What is keeping the hardware awake? And what signal are you referring to slp_s0 assertion? And what error conditions again? \n\nI don\u0027t understand about one needing to force the lid open before forcefully waking up the system. Are you referring to a lid event at the precise time of going to sleep because of lid open? And we miss that? Or is lid_open signal bouncing?",
      "parentUuid": "6ae2dd3f_8043a975",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
